			"color":"#322",
			"widgets_values":[
				"subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the young East Asian man from <Picture 1>, preserving his exact face, pale skin, tousled short black hair, slim tall build, light taupe-grey button-up shirt with rolled sleeves, black trousers, and black leather shoes.\n<Subject 2> is the young East Asian woman from <Picture 2>, preserving her exact face, long wavy dark-brown hair, slim build, cream ribbed long-sleeve sweater, and white pleated skirt.\n<Subject 3> is the cream-orange Scottish Fold cat from <Picture 3>, preserving its folded ears, round golden eyes, white chest and paws, plush tail, and red-and-white houndstooth bow tie.\n<Subject 4> is a warm modern café at night with a large window on frame-left, walnut tables in the center, a service counter in the rear center, and the entrance on rear-right.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] An eight-second 16:9 live-action romantic-comedy hook shows <Subject 3> tripping <Subject 2>, while <Subject 1> catches her just before they fall into an accidental kiss.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears throughout): fully_preserved - exact male identity, hairstyle, outfit, proportions, and gentle demeanor are retained.\n<Subject 2> (appears throughout): fully_preserved - exact female identity, hair, cream sweater, white skirt, and delicate appearance are retained.\n<Subject 3> (appears at 00:00.700-00:03.000): fully_preserved - folded ears, cream-orange fur, golden eyes, white paws, and bow tie remain visible.\n<Subject 4> (appears throughout): fully_preserved - café landmarks, warm-right key light, and cool-left window fill remain stable.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target is 16:9 cinematic live-action with polished romantic-comedy pacing, realistic anatomy, shallow depth of field, and no visible text except the specified hook caption.\n\n[Shot 1] A waist-high tracking shot follows <Subject 2> from frame-left toward center as she turns away from the rear counter carrying one cup of coffee and one small cake on a round tray. <Subject 1> sits at the adjacent table on frame-right.\n\nAt 00:00.700, <Subject 3> bursts from under the center table and darts left-to-right across her path; its folded ears, white paws, cream-orange fur, and red-and-white bow tie are clearly readable.\n\nAt 00:01.300, <Subject 2>'s front foot catches behind the cat. Her eyes widen, her shoulders pitch forward, and her long hair and white pleated skirt follow through naturally. The tray tilts, but the cake remains on its plate and the cup does not fly away. The camera adds a slight Dutch angle and a quick small push-in to emphasize the sudden imbalance.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.200, the camera cuts to a wider side angle. <Subject 1> rises rapidly from frame-right, catches <Subject 2> around the waist with one arm, and supports her forearm with the other. The cup produces one small controlled splash but remains on the tray. Their hands, arms, and bodies remain anatomically correct, without merging or deformation.\n\nAt 00:03.000, the movement shifts into elegant slow motion. The camera makes a small, slow arc around them while their faces stop only a few centimeters apart. <Subject 2> remains on frame-left and <Subject 1> on frame-right. Their eyes lock. Their lips almost touch but never make contact. Both hold their breath as the café background falls into soft bokeh.\n\nAt 00:05.200, the shot cuts to an extreme close-up alternating between their eyes and the tiny gap between their lips. <Subject 2> (S1) says in a soft, slightly breathless young female off-screen voiceover, <d>[Chinese] 被猫绊倒的瞬间，我和陌生人差点亲上了。</d> while her on-screen lips remain completely closed.\n\nFrom 00:05.500 to 00:08.000, display the exact lower-third caption “被猫绊倒的瞬间，我和陌生人差点亲上了” in clean white Chinese characters with a thin dark shadow.\n\nEnd with <Subject 1> still supporting <Subject 2>, woman frame-left and man frame-right, their faces close and their eyes locked. Preserve the exact identities, facial features, hairstyles, clothing, and body proportions from the reference pictures. No actual kiss, no extra people in focus, no identity drift, no clothing changes, no extra fingers, no fused limbs, no duplicated tray, no malformed cat, no additional subtitles, no logo, and no watermark.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nSoft café chatter and distant cup clinks continue beneath the sharp patter of cat paws, a shoe scuff, a restrained coffee splash, fabric movement, and a synchronized breath catch at the near-kiss.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA light pizzicato-string pulse begins immediately, pauses on a soft cymbal swell during the slow-motion catch, then holds one suspended piano note under the eye contact."
